<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>Who operates this site</h2>
  <p>SecretChip operates secretchip.net and the AEGIS PDNS resolver service from Europe. Privacy contact: <a href="#" data-rot13-mailto="uryyb@frpergpuvc.arg" data-subject="Privacy">hello@secretchip.net</a>.</p>
</div>

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>What this notice covers</h2>
  <p>This notice describes how SecretChip processes data in connection with this website, the contact form, the AEGIS PDNS resolver, and related services that depend on the same infrastructure.</p>
</div>

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>Categories of data we may process</h2>
  <ul class="list">
    <li>Contact form data — name, email, message content, and topic selection.</li>
    <li>Technical website logs — request metadata such as IP address, user agent, and timestamps.</li>
    <li>DNS resolver technical data — see <em>AEGIS PDNS resolver data</em> below.</li>
    <li>Security and abuse metadata — signals collected to detect and respond to misuse.</li>
    <li>Consent preferences — choices recorded through the cookie banner and preferences page.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>Why we process data</h2>
  <ul class="list">
    <li>Service delivery — operating the website and the AEGIS PDNS resolver.</li>
    <li>Security and abuse prevention — protecting users and infrastructure from misuse.</li>
    <li>Support — responding to inquiries submitted through the contact form or email.</li>
    <li>Filtering quality — improving the accuracy of AEGIS PDNS protective filtering.</li>
    <li>Legal obligations — meeting record-keeping, security, and regulatory requirements.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>Legal bases</h2>
  <p>Processing is supported by contract necessity, legitimate interests in operating and securing the service, consent where required for optional cookies and embedded forms, and legal obligations.</p>
</div>

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>Recipients and processors</h2>
  <p>SecretChip uses authorized service providers under contract to operate parts of the service. Examples include Tally for contact form delivery and infrastructure providers that host the website and the resolver. Personal data may be disclosed to regulators where required by law.</p>
</div>

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>AEGIS PDNS resolver data</h2>
  <p>DNS queries sent to the AEGIS PDNS resolver are processed by SecretChip infrastructure. Resolver operation may involve technical logs that include:</p>
  <ul class="list">
    <li>Source IP address.</li>
    <li>Timestamp.</li>
    <li>Queried domain.</li>
    <li>Query type.</li>
    <li>Resolver endpoint used (filtered or open).</li>
    <li>Policy decision (allowed, blocked, or observed).</li>
    <li>Response code.</li>
    <li>Security and abuse metadata associated with the request.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Resolver logs are used for service operation, abuse prevention, debugging, security monitoring, and improving filtering quality. <strong>SecretChip does not sell DNS query data.</strong> Filtering decisions are best-effort and may produce false positives or false negatives; users can report these and submit privacy questions through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
</div>

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>International transfers</h2>
  <p>Where international transfers occur, SecretChip relies on safeguards permitted under applicable data protection law, including standard contractual clauses where appropriate.</p>
</div>

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>Logs and personal data are retained only for as long as necessary for service operation, security, abuse prevention, troubleshooting, and legal obligations. Older records are deleted or anonymized.</p>
</div>

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You may request access, correction, deletion, restriction, objection, or portability where applicable. See <a href="/legal/privacy-requests/">Privacy Requests</a> for the submission process.</p>
</div>

<div class="legal-section">
  <h2>Complaints</h2>
  <p>Contact SecretChip first. You may also lodge a complaint with your local data protection authority.</p>
</div>
